WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.005 --> 00:00:13.562
ANTMICRO BASEBOARD · SOLUTION
New converter, reflowed ferrite
Diagnosis: the 3.3 V converter U2 is dead, and input ferrite FB1 has a cracked joint that opens when the board flexes.
Tools: Desolder wick (4) · Select (1) · Soldering iron (3) · Multimeter (2)

2
00:00:18.589 --> 00:00:30.442
STEP 1 · REMOVE U2
Wick (4) U2 off its pads.
Why: On a real board you would use hot air for a multi-pin IC, then clean the pads with wick and flux.

3
00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:38.599
STEP 2 · FIT A NEW ONE
Select the empty footprint and fit a new converter from the Inspector.

4
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.964
STEP 2 · CHECK
3.3 V at C26: +3.301 V.

5
00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:59.283
STEP 3 · CURE THE INTERMITTENT
FB1 opens when the board flexes. Soldering iron (3): reflow its joint, even though it conducts right now.
Why: A cracked joint can touch at rest and separate under stress. Reflowing re-forms the joint; waiting for it to fail on the bench wastes time.

6
00:00:59.284 --> 00:01:14.737
STEP 4 · VERIFY
Run the test bench (Run tests).
Why: It powers the board, checks every objective, and only decrypts the flag if the circuit now matches the original design: a fix that merely works around a fault does not count.

7
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.344
STEP 4 · VERIFY
All objectives pass and the flag is captured. Earn your own: it is blurred here.
